{"step_index":316,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-24T07:35:17Z","model":"gemini-3.8-flash-high","input_tokens":2259,"cache_read_tokens":162275,"output_tokens":2795,"content":"### Advanced Chess Gameplay Features — Implementation & Verification Report\n\nAll 10 advanced chess gameplay features have been implemented, synchronized with the Stockfish WebAssembly engine, and verified with an individual automated test suite.\n\n---\n\n### Feature Breakdown & Architecture\n\n```\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                        STOCKFISH CHESS ARENA                           │\n│ ┌──────────────────────┐  ┌──────────────────┐  ┌────────────────────┐ │\n│ │  Competitor Cards    │  │ Centered Board   │  │ Engine Telemetry   │ │\n│ │  - Stockfish GM      │  │ - react-board    │  │ - Depth / NPS      │ │\n│ │  - Player Clock      │  │ - Square Lights  │  │ - Eval Score / PV  │ │\n│ │  - Configurable Clock│  │ - Hint Overlay   │  │ Difficulty Presets │ │\n│ └──────────────────────┘  └──────────────────┘  │ Captured Pieces    │ │\n│ ┌──────────────────────┐  ┌──────────────────┐  │ Move History (SAN) │ │\n│ │  Arena Match Info    │  │ Action Controls  │  │ - Copy / Download  │ │\n│ │  - WebAssembly       │  │ - New Game Modal │  └────────────────────┘ │\n│ │  - Real-time UCI     │  │ - Undo / Hint    │  ┌────────────────────┐ │\n│ └──────────────────────┘  │ - Flip / Resign  │  │ Promotion Dialog   │ │\n│                           └──────────────────┘  └────────────────────┘ │\n└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n#### 1. Undo Move\n* **Dual-Scenario Reversion**:\n  * **When it is the player's turn**: Undoes 2 half-moves (the AI's last move and the player's move) so it is the player's turn again at their previous position.\n  * **When Stockfish is calculating**: Immediately calls `stopThinking()` to terminate the pending engine search, clear the watchdog timer, and revert the single player move that triggered the search.\n* **Engine Synchronization**: Re-synchronizes the board FEN with Stockfish via `position fen <reverted_fen>`, ensuring engine evaluation hashes match the board state.\n* **Game Over Recovery**: If undo is invoked following checkmate or stalemate, the game status is reset to `'in_progress'`.\n\n#### 2. Stockfish Hint (Position-Preserving Analysis)\n* **Zero Position Disruption**: Stockfish evaluates the current FEN via `position fen <fen>` and `go depth <N>` in a separate analysis request without touching `chess.js` board state.\n* **Visual Presentation**:\n  * Glowing emerald highlight on the recommended piece's `from` and destination `to` square.\n  * Floating banner indicating:\n    * Piece and standard algebraic notation (e.g. `Hint: Nf3 (g1 → f3)`)\n    * Current position evaluation score (e.g. `+1.20`)\n    * **\"Play Move\" button** to execute the suggested move directly.\n    * **\"Dismiss\" button** to clear the visual hint.\n\n#### 3. Move History (Standard Algebraic Notation & PGN Export)\n* **SAN Notation**: Renders standard chess notation (`e4`, `Nf3`, `Bxc6`, `O-O`, `Qxf7#`).\n* **Paired Turn Layout**: 2-column numbered table (`1. e4 e5`, `2. Nf3 Nc6`, etc.) with auto-scrolling to the latest ply.\n* **PGN Tools**:\n  * Single-click **Copy PGN** to clipboard.\n  * **Download `.pgn` file** with timestamped filename for analysis in external software (e.g., Lichess, Chess.com).\n\n#### 4. Board Flip & Color Perspective\n* **Interactive Perspective Toggle**: \"Flip\" button switches orientation between White and Black at any point.\n* **Play as Black Support**: When starting a game as Black, the board automatically inverts, and Stockfish immediately initiates turn 1 as White.\n\n#### 5. New Game Reset\n* **Modal Configuration**: The \"New Game\" button opens an interactive modal with:\n  * **Side Selection**: White, Black, or Random (50/50 chance).\n  * **Time Control Selection**: Bullet, Blitz, Rapid, Classical, Casual (no timer), or Custom.\n  * **Difficulty Presets**: Beginner, Easy, Medium, Hard, Expert.\n* **Complete State Reset**: Clears `chess.js` history, captured pieces, clocks, sends `ucinewgame` and `isready` to Stockfish, and starts the opening move if the AI plays White.\n\n#### 6. AI Difficulty Configuration\n* Configurable before starting a new match or adjusted on-the-fly from the right-hand panel:\n  * **Beginner**: Depth 3 plies · UCI Skill Level 2 · ~500ms\n  * **Easy**: Depth 6 plies · UCI Skill Level 7 · ~800ms\n  * **Medium**: Depth 10 plies · UCI Skill Level 13 · ~1,200ms\n  * **Hard**: Depth 14 plies · UCI Skill Level 18 · ~2,000ms\n  * **Expert**: Depth 18 plies · UCI Skill Level 20 · ~3,000ms\n  * **Custom**: Fine-grain search depth slider (1–20) and time limit slider (100–5,000ms).\n* Commands `setoption name Skill Level value <N>` dispatched over UCI to calibrate engine search depth.\n\n#### 7. Configurable Chess Clocks & Time Controls\n* **Time Controls Supported**:\n  * **Bullet**: 1 min, 2 | 1\n  * **Blitz**: 3 | 2, 5 min, 5 | 3\n  * **Rapid**: 10 min (standard), 15 | 10\n  * **Classical**: 30 min\n  * **Casual / Unlimited**: Clock disabled (renders `∞` symbol)\n  * **Custom**: User-defined base minutes (1–90m) + increment (0–60s)\n* **Increment Mechanics**: Automatically credits the increment seconds to the active player's clock upon move completion.\n* **Timeout Resolution**: If either clock hits `00:00`, the game is forfeited on time.\n\n#### 8. Captured Pieces & Material Advantage\n* Real-time calculation of missing pieces for White and Black.\n* Sorted piece icons (`♙`, `♘`, `♗`, `♖`, `♕`).\n* Dynamic material point differential badge (e.g. `White +8` or `Black +2`) updated on every capture.\n\n#### 9. Game Results & Adjudication\n* Evaluates all ending conditions natively through `chess.js`:\n  * **Check**: Non-blocking warning pill + radial red king aura.\n  * **Checkmate**: Displays victory or defeat banner with play rematch button.\n  * **Stalemate**: Automatic draw recognition.\n  * **Threefold Repetition**: Automatic draw recognition after 3 identical positions.\n  * **Insufficient Material**: Automatic draw (K vs K, K+B vs K, K+N vs K, etc.).\n  * **50-Move Rule**: Automatic draw recognition.\n  * **Timeout**: Forfeit banner identifying winner on time.\n  * **Resign**: Dedicated \"Resign\" button for human forfeiture.\n\n#### 10. Pawn Promotion & Underpromotion\n* **Interactive Promotion Dialog**: When a pawn steps onto the 8th rank (White) or 1st rank (Black), execution pauses and prompts the user to choose:\n  * **Queen** (`q`), **Rook** (`r`), **Bishop** (`b`), or **Knight** (`n`).\n* **Piece Color Matching**: Modal renders piece glyphs matching the player's active army color.\n* **Engine Underpromotion Parsing**: Supports Stockfish promotions (such as `e7e8q` or `c2c1n`), correctly applying underpromotions to the board.\n\n---\n\n### Automated Individual Feature Test Verification\n\nAll 10 features were tested individually using [test-all-features.cjs](file:///C:/Users/DELL/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/stockfish-chess-arena/test-all-features.cjs):\n\n```text\n===============================================================\n🧪 STOCKFISH CHESS ARENA: ADVANCED FEATURES VERIFICATION SUITE\n===============================================================\n\n[FEATURE 1] Testing Undo Move functionality...\n  ✓ History has 2 moves (e4, e5)\n  ✓ Turn is White after 2 moves\n  ✓ History empty after 2-step undo\n  ✓ FEN restored to start position\n  ✓ Turn is White\n  ✓ Human played d4\n  ✓ Reverted 1-step undo successfully\n✅ FEATURE 1 PASSED: Undo Move\n\n[FEATURE 3] Testing Move History & SAN Notation...\n  ✓ Executed move e4\n  ✓ Executed move e5\n  ✓ Executed move Nf3\n  ✓ Executed move Nc6\n  ✓ Executed move Bb5\n  ✓ Executed move a6\n  ✓ Executed move Bxc6\n  ✓ Executed move dxc6\n  ✓ 8 moves in history\n  ✓ Algebraic notation: Bb5\n  ✓ Capture notation: Bxc6\n  ✓ PGN format valid\n✅ FEATURE 3 PASSED: Move History & SAN Notation\n\n[FEATURE 4] Testing Board Flip & Perspective...\n  ✓ Orientation flipped to black\n  ✓ Orientation flipped back to white\n  ✓ When player is Black, Stockfish (White) moves first\n✅ FEATURE 4 PASSED: Board Flip & Perspective\n\n[FEATURE 5] Testing New Game Reset...\n  ✓ Game in progress\n  ✓ Board state reset\n  ✓ History cleared\n  ✓ Turn reset to White\n  ✓ Game over flag cleared\n✅ FEATURE 5 PASSED: New Game Reset\n\n[FEATURE 7] Testing Chess Clocks & Increments...\n  ✓ White time updated with -4s + 2s increment: 178s\n  ✓ Black time updated with -5s + 2s increment: 177s\n  ✓ Timeout detected when clock hits 0\n✅ FEATURE 7 PASSED: Configurable Chess Clocks\n\n[FEATURE 8] Testing Captured Pieces & Material Differential...\n  ✓ 2 White pawns captured\n  ✓ Black Queen captured by White\n  ✓ White has material advantage after winning Black Queen (+8)\n✅ FEATURE 8 PASSED: Captured Pieces & Material Advantage\n\n[FEATURE 9] Testing Game Results (Checkmate, Stalemate, Draws)...\n  ✓ Scholar Mate: isCheckmate() is true\n  ✓ isGameOver() is true\n  ✓ Stalemate detected\n  ✓ isGameOver() is true on stalemate\n  ✓ King vs King: insufficient material detected\n  ✓ Threefold repetition detected\n✅ FEATURE 9 PASSED: Game Results Detection\n\n[FEATURE 10] Testing Pawn Promotion & Underpromotion...\n  ✓ Promoted pawn to Queen on f8\n  ✓ Piece on f8 is Queen\n  ✓ Underpromoted pawn to Knight on f8\n  ✓ Piece on f8 is Knight\n✅ FEATURE 10 PASSED: Pawn Promotion & Underpromotion\n\n[FEATURE 2 & 6] Testing Live Stockfish Hint and Difficulty via UCI...\n  [UCI] Received uciok\n[FEATURE 6] Testing UCI Difficulty Skill Level adjustment...\n  ✓ Skill Level option accepted by Stockfish\n✅ FEATURE 6 PASSED: Difficulty Configuration\n\n[FEATURE 2] Testing Stockfish Hint calculation without altering position...\n  Position FEN before hint: r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p3/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 2 3\n  ✓ St